# core.autocrlf is on for this repository, which is right for the source and
# wrong for anything that is not text: git announced that it would replace LF
# with CRLF inside records/sources/sos-clerks-and-polling-places.pdf, which would have
# committed a corrupted document and only shown up when somebody tried to
# open it. These are bytes, not lines.
*.pdf   -text
*.png   -text
*.ico   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.webp  -text
*.gz    -text
*.zip   -text
# The Secretary of State's results spreadsheets in records/sources/, whose
# sha256 collected/election_<year>.json names (17 October 2026).
*.xls   -text
*.xlsx  -text
# The text canary's fixtures (tests/documents/README.md): the laptop's own
# text of four documents, kept as the bytes the laptop wrote, line ends and
# all, whatever a checkout is set to convert.
tests/documents/*.txt   -text

# And these are text, everywhere, whatever the checkout does: the version
# stamps and the palette are compared byte for byte by preflight.
*.py    text
*.js    text
*.css   text
*.html  text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.svg   text
*.csv   text
